      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T13:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: I think we don\u0027t need to require clients to explicitly assign TextureBinding to the MSAA texture. We could just implicitly use `Texture::AddInternalUsage(TextureBinding)` if it is multisampled and DawnPartialLoadResolveTexture is enabled.\n\nThe reason it is needed for expanding is because Vulkan needs it for subpass inputs\u0027 usage and the subpass inputs\u0027 usage might not be optimal. However, for partial resolve, I think we can use Vulkan API\u0027s renderArea option directly (if we want to enable this feature in Vulkan in future), no need for additional usage. For other backends, we can just unconditionally AddInternalUsage(TextureBinding).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 232,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 246
      },
      "revId": "3541712d3f447b02d6fc90a82858eb601dbfaf21",
